  "bodyTypst": "Let $f$ be the function given by $f(x)= frac(2 x,1 + x^(2))$.\n\n(a) Write the first four nonzero terms and the general term of the Taylor series for $f$ about $x = 0$.\n\n(b) Does the series found in part (a), when evaluated at $x = 1$, converge to $f(1)$ ? Explain why or why not.\n\n(c) The derivative of $ln lr((1 + x^(2)))$ is $frac(2 x,1 + x^(2))$. Write the first four nonzero terms of the Taylor series for $ln lr((1 + x^(2)))$ about $x = 0$.\n\n(d) Use the series found in part (c) to find a rational number $A$ such that $lr(| A - ln lr((frac(5,4)))|)< frac(1,100)$. Justify your answer.",
